---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Your privacy"
  lede="Looking up cancer information is personal. Hausla is designed so that we don't need to know who you are, and we don't try to find out."
  updated="2026-11-11"
>
  <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, no sign-up, no forms that ask about your health.</li>
    <li>No advertising, no analytics and no tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>No third-party fonts, trackers or embedded social media on our pages.</li>
    <li>Anything you save (when saving pages arrives) stays on your own device.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing about you, directly.</strong> Hausla is a set of plain web pages. We don't ask for your name, phone
    number, email, location or medical details, and the site does not set cookies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Our hosting provider</h2>
  <p>
    Hausla is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like most web hosts, GitHub may record technical
    information when you visit, such as your IP address, for security and to keep the service running. We don't
    receive or use this information. You can read
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="device">What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    When we add features like saving pages for later, the list of what you saved will be kept only in your browser's
    storage on your own device. It is never sent to us. You can clear it at any time by clearing your browser's site
    data. Today, Hausla stores nothing on your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you share a phone or computer and want to keep your browsing private, consider using your browser's private or
    incognito mode.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    When you follow a link to another website, such as a hospital, government portal or community, that website's own
    privacy practices apply. Some, especially social media and forums, may track visitors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="future">If this ever changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever introduce anything that involves personal information (for example, a form to share your story), we
    will collect only what is necessary, explain clearly why and how it is used, ask for your consent, and follow
    India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. This page will be updated first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, write to <Contact />.</p>
</Page>
